    "generation_method": "Curated from established literary canons including Harold Bloom's Western Canon, Modern Library lists, university core curricula (Columbia, UChicago, St. John's), and consensus among major literary historians and critics",
    "significance": "These authors define the core of world literature. Their works have shaped literary traditions, influenced countless writers, and remain central to understanding human culture and artistic expression across eras.",
    "scoring_rationale": "Pre-1970 works by these authors receive a 30-point canonical baseline to ensure they compete fairly with contemporary award winners, as most major literary awards and 'best-of' lists were created in the 1990s-2020s, creating systematic bias against earlier masterpieces."
